.Dd September 30, 2026
.Dt R2PM 1
.Sh NAME
.Nm r2pm
.Nd Radare2 Package Manager
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm r2pm
.Op Fl AabcdeHhijlpqrRstuUvw
.Op Ar pkgs...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The package manager for Radare2, allowing installation, update, uninstallation, and discovery of plugins and tools.
.Bl -tag -width Fl
.It Fl A
Include packages unsupported by the local platform or build in
.Fl s
results.
Text output marks them as
.Ql [unsupported] .
.It Fl a Ar repository
Add or delete external repository. Using '-a repository' adds a repository, and '-a -repository' deletes it. Use with no arguments to list all registered repos.
.It Fl b
Require a binary package for the target architecture, operating system and
.Ev R2V
version.
Use with
.Fl i .
Skip source checkout and build dependencies.
If no binary installer exists or installation fails, return an error and
request re-running without
.Fl b ;
never fall back to building from source.
.It Fl c Ar pkgname
Clear cached sources for the given package. Use
.Fl cp
to clean the user plugin directory
.It Fl d, Cm doc Ar pkgname
Show documentation and source for given package script
.It Fl e Ar pkgname
Edit using $EDITOR the given package script
.It Fl f
Force operation. Requires
.Fl U ,
.Fl i
or
.Fl u
.It Fl gi Ar pkg
Global install (system-wide)
.It Fl h
Display help message
.It Fl H Op variable
List all or selected r2pm environment variables
.It Fl i Ar pkgname
Install/update package and its dependencies
.It Fl I
Information about the repository and installed packages
.It Fl j
JSON output. Requires
.Fl l ,
.Fl s
or
.Fl v .
Search objects include a
.Va platforms
array of strings and a
.Va supported
boolean.
.It Fl l
List installed packages
.It Fl q
Be quiet. Requires an action
.It Fl r Ar cmd ...args
Run shell command with R2PM_BINDIR in PATH
.It Fl R Ar pkgname
Reload plugin (See R2PM_RELOAD code block package)
.It Fl s Op keyword
Search available packages in the database matching a string.
By default, filter to packages supported by the local platform and build.
Return an error code if no package was found
.It Fl t Ar YYYY-MM-DD
Set the package checkout date. Requires an action
.It Fl u Ar pkgname
Uninstall package (see -f to force uninstall)
.It Fl uci Ar pkgname
Uninstall + clean + install
.It Fl ui Ar pkgname
Uninstall + install
.It Fl U
Download/initialize or update database (-f for a clean clone)
.It Fl UU
Same as -U but upgrade all the installed r2 plugins
.It Fl v
Show version
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Pp
.Bl -tag -width Fl
.It Ev SUDO
Command to use for system-wide installs (default: sudo)
.It Ev R2PM_SUDO
Value of
.Ev SUDO
when using
.Fl g ,
empty otherwise.
Exported to package scripts.
.It Ev R2PM_GLOBAL , GLOBAL
Set to 1 when using
.Fl g ,
0 otherwise.
Exported to package scripts.
.It Ev R2PM_GITURL
Git repository for the package database
(default: https://github.com/radareorg/radare2-pm)
.It Ev R2PM_PLUGDIR
Directory for user plugins (default: ~/.local/share/radare2/plugins)
.It Ev R2PM_BINDIR
Directory for user binaries (default: ~/.local/share/radare2/prefix/bin)
.It Ev R2PM_MANDIR
Directory for user man pages (default: ~/.local/share/radare2/prefix/man)
.It Ev R2PM_DOCDIR
Directory for user documentation (default: ~/.local/share/radare2/prefix/doc)
.It Ev R2PM_OFFLINE
Disable online operations (default: 0)
.It Ev R2V
Release version requested by binary installers (defaults to the installed
.Cm radare2 -qv
version).
.It Ev R2PM_OS
Target operating system exported to package scripts
(for example linux, darwin or windows).
.It Ev R2PM_ARCH
Target architecture exported to package scripts (for example x86 or arm).
.It Ev R2PM_BITS
Target pointer size exported to package scripts (32 or 64).
.It Ev R2PM_TRIPLET
Target platform triplet exported to package scripts as
.Ar os-arch-bits
(for example linux-x86-64 or darwin-arm-64).
.It Ev R2PM_PLATFORM
Override the platform used to filter
.Fl s
results. Accepted values are
.Cm r2 ,
.Cm unix ,
.Cm windows ,
.Cm qjs ,
and
.Cm any ;
multiple values may be space-separated.
Packages with an
.Ic R2PM_INSTALL_R2()
block are portable radare2-command packages; the automatically detected platform
always includes
.Cm r2 .
The block is executed by radare2 during installation; a matching
.Ic R2PM_UNINSTALL_R2()
block handles uninstallation.
.It Ev R2PM_DBDIR
Directory for r2pm database (default: ~/.local/share/radare2/r2pm/db)
.It Ev R2PM_GITDIR
Directory for git repositories (default: ~/.local/share/radare2/r2pm/git)
.It Ev R2PM_GITSKIP
Skip git pull operations when set
.It Ev R2PM_TIME
Point in time to use for git checkout (format: YYYY-MM-DD)
.It Ev R2_LOG_LEVEL
Control verbosity of log messages
.It Ev R2PM_INCDIR
Directory for include files
.It Ev R2PM_LIBDIR
Directory for libraries
.It Ev R2PM_PREFIX
Installation prefix
.It Ev R2_CFLAGS
Compiler flags to build against radare2 libraries
.It Ev R2_LDFLAGS
Linker search path flags to build against radare2 libraries
.It Ev R2_LIBS
Library flags to link against radare2 libraries
.It Ev R2_LIBEXT
Shared library extension for plugins (so, dylib or dll)
.It Ev R2_USER_PLUGINS
User plugin directory, regardless of
.Fl g
.El
.Sh BINARY PACKAGES
Packages implement
.Ic R2PM_BINSTALL()
as a shell script on Unix, or
.Ic R2PM_BINSTALL_WINDOWS()
as Windows commands.
These blocks run without a source checkout; they must select an exact release
using
.Ev R2V , R2PM_OS , R2PM_ARCH
and
.Ev R2PM_BITS ,
download and install its files, and return a nonzero status on failure.
Unix scripts run with
.Ql set -e
and can call
.Ic R2PM_FAIL Ar message
to abort with an error.
On Windows the block lines are joined with
.Ql &&
and run by
.Cm cmd ,
so each line must be a single command.
The binary installer handles its own tools and runtime dependencies;
.Ic R2PM_NEEDS
and
.Ic R2PM_DEPS
are used only for source installs.
Normal installation directories,
.Ev GLOBAL
and
.Ev R2PM_SUDO
are available.
Installations are registered only on success, and marked as binary.
.Pp
Packages installed this way are uninstalled with
.Ic R2PM_BUNINSTALL()
or
.Ic R2PM_BUNINSTALL_WINDOWS() ,
which run the same way and must remove the files the binary installer added;
.Fl u
selects them automatically, without
.Fl b .
If the package has no such block,
.Ic R2PM_UNINSTALL()
is used.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Pp
Install a package
.Pp
  $ r2pm -i yara3
.Pp
Install the r2frida binary matching the installed radare2 version
.Pp
  $ r2pm -bi r2frida
.Pp
Select a binary release explicitly (for example in CI)
.Pp
  $ R2V=6.2.2 r2pm -bi r2frida
.Pp
Clean cache and then install (don't git pull on $R2PM_GITDIR/yara3)
.Pp
  $ r2pm -ci yara3
.Pp
Avoid init/update calls (don't git pull on $R2PM_DBDIR)
.Pp
  $ R2PM_OFFLINE=1 r2pm -i yara
.Pp
Uninstall a package
.Pp
  $ r2pm -u yara3
.Pp
Force uninstall a package
.Pp
  $ r2pm -fu yara3
.Pp
Search a package
.Pp
  $ r2pm -s yara
.Pp
Search all packages, including unsupported ones
.Pp
  $ r2pm -As
.Pp
List installed packages
.Pp
  $ r2pm -l
.Pp
Update database and upgrade all installed packages
.Pp
  $ r2pm -UU
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Pp
.Xr radare2(1)
